+# Public sanitized plugin-record example
+
+## Public evidence boundary
+
+These records bind 14 inert, sanitized `.txt` fixture files, not installed plugins.
+The manifest digest binds only the public `SHA256SUMS.plugins` subset.
+Deployment identities, account numbers, personal paths and private provenance
+have been replaced; the approval fields are explicit illustrative placeholders.
+No original private archive review or live enrollment is certified here.
+
+## Registry and source closure
+
+The unchanged version-1 registry maps plugin keys to relative paths and SHA256s.
+The example preserves the original public API identifiers for compatibility.
+The GitHub-read fixture includes its entry point, credential helper,
+read helper and plugin manifest. The project-work fixture includes its entry
+point and client, config, errors, ingress, native, runtime, service and store
+helpers plus its plugin manifest. Every recorded digest is re-derived from
+the sanitized public bytes; the fixture manifest and registry agree.
+
+## Tests and limitations
+
+Source tests check fixture membership, per-file hashes, registry equality,
+placeholder provenance, positive file validation and one-byte rejection.
+The mirror separately verifies the normalized complete source tree.
+These are inert fixture tests: no plugin or service is invoked by them.
+They neither validate the original private archive nor authorize deployment.
+The actual plugin attestation path still requires independently reviewed
+bytes, boot/disk custody, managed dependency custody and its deadline checks.
+The enclosing application and installed plugins are not approved by this example.
+
+## Applying
+
+Use the complete snapshot replay and mandatory regex repair in the mirror README.
+Do not treat public placeholder approval fields as deployment authority.
+
